; fakereal_full.def — exports of the fake real DLL (Win32 harness only).
; The 3 stdcall names MUST match what gshim.c resolves
; ("_grBufferSwap@4" etc.); fakereal_counts is the harness-only
; interrogation export. Missing-one-export variants are generated by
; build-harness.sh (this file minus one line each), so the fake keeps
; its code but loses the export — GetProcAddress then fails exactly
; like a real DLL lacking that symbol.
; MINGW-32 LINK RULE (same F-3 rule as gshim.def, 2026-10-11):
; explicit-alias form with the internal name EXACTLY the decorated
; symbol (WITH the leading underscore). A mismatched internal is ALSO
; exported by MinGW-32 (38+3 twins on the shim). Variant generation
; (grep -vF '_gr...@N') still matches, since the decorated name stays
; on its own line.
LIBRARY glide2x_gex_real
EXPORTS
    "_grBufferSwap@4"=_grBufferSwap@4
    "_grBufferNumPending@0"=_grBufferNumPending@0
    "_grGlideShutdown@0"=_grGlideShutdown@0
    "_fakereal_counts@16"=_fakereal_counts@16
